      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your advice.\n\n@Ben I also noticed that gn/skia/BUILD.gn does have cross-compilation support, but it only supports android, ios, mac, and fuchisa systems, not linux. Maybe we should find a better way to meet different needs.\n\nThis CL provide a way，for example ones build arm64 in linux x86-64 platform: \n./buildtools/linux64/gn gen out/arm64_Release \u0027--args\u003dis_debug\u003dfalse is_official_build\u003dfalse target_cpu \u003d \"arm64\" skia_sysroot \u003d \"/mnt/sysroot/linux/debian_bullseye_arm64-sysroot\" skia_cross_target \u003d \"aarch64-linux-gnu\"\u0027\n\n@brian  Yes, those extra_xxxflags also can. But now the skia build system lacks an entry to specify sysroot and target flags where current_os \u003d\u003d \"linux\".",
